Create a basic Express app in a file named `app.js`:
```js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const PORT = 3000;

app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.send('Hello from Express!');
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```
Run the app with `node app.js` and visit `http://localhost:3000` in your browser to see the message.
